@scene chapter_1b_wisdom_of_system

background: dragon_celestial.jpg
music: wisdom_theme.mp3

dialogue:
"The dragon folds its enormous wings."
"The golden eyes that judged your soul begin to dim."

npc Dragon:
"Power alone cannot shape destiny, {{player_name}}."
"You carry {{hp}} health and {{strength}} strength."
"But you do not yet know what those numbers ARE."

background: sky_summons.jpg

dialogue:
"The dragon raises one massive claw toward the sky."
"A pillar of light erupts from the ground beneath you."
"The mountains dissolve. The clouds scatter."
"Even the dragon breaks apart into countless golden fragments."
"..."
"Darkness."
"..."

background: ancient_library.png

dialogue:
"A single blue light appears in the distance. It grows closer."
"An endless hall materializes around you."
"Shelves of glowing books stretch farther than the eye can see."

background: sage_reading.jpg

dialogue:
"At the center sits a robed figure, hooded, an open book resting across his knees."

background: mysterious_figure

npc ???:
"Welcome, {{player_name}}."
"You survived the Trial of the Dragon."
"Now you must understand the power you wield."

dialogue:
"The figure lowers his hood."
"White hair. A weathered face. Eyes that have read more than any one life should hold."

system skill_learned:
"MODULE UNLOCKED"
"WISDOM OF THE SYSTEM"
"Variables · Data Types · print() · input()"

background: system_sage

npc System Sage:
"I am the Sage of the System."
"Every soul that passes the Dragon arrives here."
"Look — the words you spoke at your Awakening."

dialogue:
"He opens his hand."
"Your character sheet unfurls in the air, exactly as you wrote it."

interactive: wisdom_character_sheet

npc System Sage:
"Do you know what these symbols truly are?"

background: ancient_library.png

dialogue:
"You shake your head."
"The Sage smiles, and the hall answers him."
"— LESSON I — MEMORIES OF THE WORLD —"

dialogue:
"One line drifts forward, glowing."
"It folds itself into a small wooden chest."
"A name burns itself into the lid."
"The value falls inside. The lid closes."
"Click."

npc System Sage:
"Every piece of information must have a place to rest."
"This chest is a Variable."
"A name on the lid. A value within."
"Open them. See what your world remembers."

interactive: wisdom_open_chests

npc System Sage:
"Without variables, no hero remembers their name."
"No warrior remembers their strength."
"No kingdom remembers its history."
"Variables are the memory of this world."

dialogue:
"The Sage sets an empty chest before you. Its lid is bare."

npc System Sage:
"A chest is not born with a name."
"You give it one, and you fill it — with a single stroke."
"The equals sign does not mean 'is the same as'."
"It means 'place this inside'."
"Try it. Forge a chest of your own."

interactive: wisdom_assignment_forge

npc System Sage:
"Good. And what is placed may be replaced."
"Assign again, and the old value is simply... forgotten."

interactive: wisdom_reassign

dialogue:
"The chest's contents flicker, then settle on the new value."
"The old one is gone, as if it had never been."
"— LESSON II — THE NATURE OF INFORMATION —"

npc System Sage:
"Not all values share the same nature."
"Your name is not the same KIND of thing as your health."
"Watch. The System will read each one."

interactive: wisdom_type_scan

npc System Sage:
"Four families. Every value the System knows belongs to one."
"Text wrapped in quotation marks — a String."
"Whole numbers — an Integer."
"Numbers that fracture into decimals — a Float."
"And truth itself, which has only two faces — a Boolean."

dialogue:
"Four runes ignite and begin to orbit you."
"String — Integer — Float — Boolean"

npc System Sage:
"Now sort them yourself."
"A merchant who mistakes a name for a number loses his fortune."

interactive: wisdom_sort_types

npc System Sage:
"You see it now."
"The quotation mark is a boundary."
"Cross it, and 250 stops being a quantity and becomes mere shapes on a page."

interactive: wisdom_quote_trap

background: sage_reading.jpg

dialogue:
"— LESSON III — THE VOICE OF THE SYSTEM —"
"The Sage leads you to an enormous silver mirror."
"It reflects nothing at all. Only darkness."

npc You:
"Why can't I see myself?"

npc System Sage:
"Because the mirror cannot read your thoughts."
"You hold values, but you have never once SPOKEN them."
"There is a spell for this."

dialogue:
"A command burns itself into the air."
"print()"

npc System Sage:
"Place something inside the brackets."
"The System will reveal it to the world."
"But be careful what you place there."

interactive: wisdom_predict_print

npc System Sage:
"You understand the difference."
"A name inside quotes is text. A name without them is a chest — and the mirror shows what is inside."
"Now speak, {{player_name}}."
"Show the mirror your name, and your health."

mission: wisdom_voice_of_system

background: player

dialogue:
"The mirror floods with light."
"Your name blazes across its surface, then your health beneath it."
"For the first time, the world has heard you."

background: system_sage

npc System Sage:
"Well done. You have learned to speak."

system skill_learned:
"SKILL LEARNED"
"You have learned 'VOICE OF THE SYSTEM'."
"The world can now hear you speak."

dialogue:
"— LESSON IV — LISTENING TO THE WORLD —"
"The mirror vanishes."
"A luminous crystal descends in its place."

background: crystal

npc Crystal:
"Choose your weapon."

dialogue:
"..."
"Nothing happens."
"The crystal waits. You have no way to answer it."

npc System Sage:
"You have learned to speak to the world."
"But a conversation runs both ways."
"The world now wishes to speak to YOU."

dialogue:
"A second command materializes beside the first."
"input()"

npc System Sage:
"This spell does not shout. It listens."
"It halts the world, waits for an answer, and hands that answer back to you."
"And what it returns is always Text — even when it looks like a number."
"Remember that. It has undone wiser travellers than you."

interactive: wisdom_input_flow

npc System Sage:
"Now ask the crystal its question."
"Store what it hears. Then announce the answer."

mission: wisdom_listener_of_worlds

dialogue:
"A word settles into a brand-new chest, labelled weapon."
"The crystal shatters into light."
"A blade materializes and falls into your waiting hand."
"It hums with a sound like a held breath."

background: system_sage

npc System Sage:
"Excellent. You have learned to listen."

system item_obtained:
"ITEM OBTAINED"
"You have obtained 'BEGINNER'S BLADE'."

system skill_learned:
"SKILL LEARNED"
"You have learned 'LISTENER OF WORLDS'."
"The world can now answer when you ask."

npc System Sage:
"Prove it once more, and the door will open for you."
"Everything you have learned — in a single breath."

interactive: wisdom_final_recall

background: ancient_library.png

dialogue:
"The Sage closes the ancient book in his hands."
"The chests, the mirror, the orbiting runes — all of it fades."
"He turns toward a colossal stone doorway at the end of the hall."
"Three symbols are carved into it, dark and unlit."
"Fire. Water. Nature."
"The doorway trembles."
"A voice echoes from somewhere far beyond it."

npc ???:
"Traveller..."
"The world remembers your name."
"It hears your voice."
"It listens when you ask."
"But it still cannot CHOOSE."

npc System Sage:
"That lesson is not mine to give."
"Someone beyond that door has waited a very long time for you."
"Go. He is not as strong as he once was."

dialogue:
"The Sage steps aside."
"The great door grinds open, and cold forest air rushes in."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"Wisdom of the System"
"Mastered: Variables · Assignment · Data Types · print() · input()"

reward:
xp: 50
gold: 25
achievement: WISDOM OF THE SYSTEM

next:
chapter_2_trial_of_choice
